Hello,
Download the desired import function and the analysis function to the directory containing your data files

For single measurements (including temperature controlled Raman experiments)
  Import_Raman_SingleMeasurement.m
  Raman_SingleMeasurement_Analysis.m
  Raman_SingleMeasurement_Analysis_FullSpectrum.m

For time series data analysis
  Import_Raman_TimeSeries.m
  Raman_TimeSeries_Analysis.m
  Raman_TimeSeries_Analysis_FullSpectrum.m

You can select multiple files to import and the data will be stored in a MATLAB struct. You can import .txt files or .csv files

=== Single measurement data ===
Col 1 (FileName) === File name
Col 2 (Data)     === Data
  Col 2. Col 1 === Raman shifts
  Col 2. Col 2 === Raw Raman Intensity

Once the normalization is performed
  Col 2. Col 3 === Normalized Raman intensity
  Col 2. Col 4 === Normalized non-zero Raman intensity

=== Time series data ===
Col 1 (FileName)   === File name
Col 2 (RamanShift) === Raman shifts (without any intensity). This is kept for sanity checks
Col 3 (TimeOffset) === Time offset from the initial measurement at time t = 0
Col 4 (TimeStamp)  === Time stamp of each collected spectrum
Col 5 (Data)       === Data
  Col 5. Col 1     === Raman shifts
  Col 5. Col 2:end === Raw Raman Intensity

Once the normalization is performed

Col 6 (Normalized_Data) === Normalized data
  Col 6. Col 1     === Raman shifts
  Col 6. Col 2:end === Normalized Raman Intensity

Col 7 (Normalized_NonZero_Data) === Normalized nonZero data
  Col 7. Col 1     === Raman shifts
  Col 7. Col 2:end === Normalized nonZero Raman Intensity

=== Analysis files ===
I have created the analysis files for basic data analysis like plotting. Further analysis could be performed as you like.

Cheers!

All feedback is welcome!
